#: ../../../index.rst:130
msgid "Run poe from anywhere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:132
msgid ""
"By default poe will detect when you're inside a project with a pyproject."
"toml or poe_tasks file in the root. However if you want to run it from "
"elsewhere then that is supported by using the :sh:`-C/--directory` option to "
"specify an alternate location for the toml file. The task will run with the "
"given location as the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:134
msgid ""
"In all cases the path to project root (where the pyproject.toml resides) "
"will be available as :sh:`$POE_ROOT` within the command line and process. "
"The variable :sh:`$POE_PWD` contains the original working directory from "
"which poe was run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:136
msgid ""
"Using this feature you can also define :doc:`global tasks<./guides/"
"global_tasks>` that are not associated with any particular project."
msgstr ""
